# SpinbitZ Development Rules

## Core Paradigms

### FRAOP (Functional-Reactive Aspect-Oriented Programming)
- All components MUST follow the FRAOP architecture
- Use Cycle.js for reactive programming
- Use xstream for stream management
- Implement proper state management
- Follow TTDD (Test and Task Driven Development)

### MVI (Model-View-Intent)
- All components MUST implement MVI pattern
- Separate intent, model, and view logic
- Use proper stream transformations
- Maintain clear data flow
- Implement proper state management
- Follow fractal state patterns

### TTDD (Test and Task Driven Development)
- Write tests BEFORE implementation
- Follow task template structure
- Maintain test coverage > 90%
- Document all changes
- Follow review checklist
- Use proper commit messages

## Code Structure

### Component Rules
- Use functional components
- Implement proper TypeScript types
- Follow atomic design principles
- Use proper stream composition
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow accessibility guidelines

### State Management
- Use fractal state patterns
- Implement proper state isolation
- Use proper stream operators
- Follow unidirectional data flow
- Implement proper state updates
- Use proper state selection

### Stream Management
- Use xstream for streams
- Implement proper stream cleanup
- Use proper stream operators
- Handle stream errors
- Implement proper backpressure
- Use proper stream composition

